{"key":"enterprise/T1542","id":"T1542","name":"Pre-OS Boot","domain":"enterprise","level":"technique","parent_id":null,"tactics":["persistence","stealth"],"platforms":["Linux","macOS","Network Devices","Windows"],"environments":["cloud-hosted-endpoint","network-infrastructure","onprem"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"Adversaries may abuse Pre-OS Boot mechanisms as a way to establish persistence on a system. During the booting process of a computer, firmware and various startup services are loaded before the operating system. These programs control flow of execution before the operating system takes control. Adversaries may overwrite data in boot drivers or firmware such as BIOS (Basic Input/Output System) and The Unified Extensible Firmware Interface (UEFI)…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1542","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--7f0ca133-88c4-40c6-a62f-b3083a7fbc2e","source_modified":"2026-05-12T15:12:00.662Z","source_object_version":"2.0","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0064","name":"Command Execution","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0064","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--685f917a-e95e-4ba0-ade1-c7d354dae6e0","page":"telemetry/DC0064/"},{"id":"DC0054","name":"Drive Access","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0054","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--73ff2dcc-24b1-4368-b9dc-706dd9e68354","page":"telemetry/DC0054/"},{"id":"DC0046","name":"Drive Modification","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0046","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--4dcd8ba3-2075-4f8b-941e-39884ffaac08","page":"telemetry/DC0046/"},{"id":"DC0039","name":"File Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0039","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--2b3bfe19-d59a-460d-93bb-2f546adc2d2c","page":"telemetry/DC0039/"},{"id":"DC0061","name":"File Modification","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0061","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--84572de3-9583-4c73-aabd-06ea88123dd8","page":"telemetry/DC0061/"},{"id":"DC0004","name":"Firmware Modification","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0004","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--b9d031bb-d150-4fc6-8025-688201bf3ffd","page":"telemetry/DC0004/"},{"id":"DC0032","name":"Process Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0032","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3d20385b-24ef-40e1-9f56-f39750379077","page":"telemetry/DC0032/"}],"strategies":[{"id":"DET0278","name":"Detection Strategy for T1542 Pre-OS Boot","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0278","stix_id":"x-mitre-detection-strategy--abf6c96c-09f3-4bea-a5b7-1177f99881bc","relationship_id":"relationship--31295488-09cd-4a34-a7e1-88f47fdef79e"}],"analytics":[{"id":"AN0774","name":"Analytic 0774","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0278#AN0774","guidance":"Unusual modification of boot records (MBR, VBR) or EFI partitions not associated with legitimate patch cycles or OS upgrades. Registry or WMI events associated with firmware update tools executed from unexpected parent processes. API calls (e.g., DeviceIoControl) writing directly to raw disk sectors. Subsequent abnormal boot configuration changes followed by unsigned driver loads.","platforms":["Windows"],"strategy_id":"DET0278"},{"id":"AN0775","name":"Analytic 0775","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0278#AN0775","guidance":"Detection of writes to /boot or EFI directories outside of expected package manager updates. Monitoring kernel log and auditd events for attempts to overwrite bootloader binaries (e.g., grub, shim). Unexpected execution of efibootmgr or dd writing to /dev/sdX devices followed by boot parameter changes.","platforms":["Linux"],"strategy_id":"DET0278"},{"id":"AN0776","name":"Analytic 0776","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0278#AN0776","guidance":"Abnormal modification of EFI firmware binaries in /System/Library/CoreServices/ or NVRAM parameters not associated with OS updates. Unified logs capturing calls to bless or nvram commands executed from untrusted parent processes. Sudden unsigned kext loads after EFI variable tampering.","platforms":["macOS"],"strategy_id":"DET0278"},{"id":"AN0777","name":"Analytic 0777","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0278#AN0777","guidance":"Unexpected firmware image uploads via TFTP/FTP/SCP. Configuration changes modifying boot image pointers. Logs showing boot variable redirection to non-standard images. Anomalous reboots immediately following firmware changes not tied to patch schedules.","platforms":["Network Devices"],"strategy_id":"DET0278"}],"log_sources":[{"component_id":"DC0032","component":"Process Creation","name":"WinEventLog:Security","channel":"EventCode=4688","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN0774","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0278#AN0774","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0032/"},{"component_id":"DC0039","component":"File Creation","name":"WinEventLog:Sysmon","channel":"EventCode=11","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN0774","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0278#AN0774","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0039/"},{"component_id":"DC0054","component":"Drive Access","name":"WinEventLog:Sysmon","channel":"EventCode=9","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN0774","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0278#AN0774","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0054/"},{"component_id":"DC0061","component":"File Modification","name":"auditd:SYSCALL","channel":"open, write: Modification of /boot/grub/* or /boot/efi/*","platforms":["Linux"],"analytic_id":"AN0775","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0278#AN0775","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0061/"},{"component_id":"DC0064","component":"Command Execution","name":"auditd:EXECVE","channel":"exec: Execution of dd, efibootmgr, or flashrom modifying firmware/boot partitions","platforms":["Linux"],"analytic_id":"AN0775","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0278#AN0775","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0064/"},{"component_id":"DC0032","component":"Process Creation","name":"macos:unifiedlog","channel":"Execution of bless or nvram modifying boot parameters","platforms":["macOS"],"analytic_id":"AN0776","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0278#AN0776","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0032/"},{"component_id":"DC0061","component":"File Modification","name":"macos:unifiedlog","channel":"Modification of /System/Library/CoreServices/boot.efi","platforms":["macOS"],"analytic_id":"AN0776","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0278#AN0776","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0061/"},{"component_id":"DC0004","component":"Firmware Modification","name":"networkdevice:config","channel":"Boot variable modified to point to non-standard or unsigned image","platforms":["Network Devices"],"analytic_id":"AN0777","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0278#AN0777","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0004/"},{"component_id":"DC0046","component":"Drive Modification","name":"networkdevice:firmware","channel":"Unexpected firmware image upload events via TFTP/FTP/SCP","platforms":["Network Devices"],"analytic_id":"AN0777","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0278#AN0777","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0046/"}],"unresolved_references":[],"basis":"ATT&CK detects relationship → detection strategy → analytic →